A||||9||JohnnyK||Spray on paint-stripper||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||08-07-2000||04:04 PM||||Well, I have been using that green-jelly type paint stripper to remove the clearcoat from my rims, but noticed that I have to do it over and over, because I can not get a good, even coat. Has anyone tried the spray on stuff? (It was right beside this stuff in the hardware store) If it is gel-like too, I figured it would work better? Anyone ever tried this? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||GT Bastard||08-07-2000||04:21 PM||||I used the aircraft jelly stuff.  The key is to let it sit for awhile and it worked it's magic.  All I had to do was hose them down and the paint came right off.  Looked pretty nice.  This was on a set of GTA rims(honeycomb style.)||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||08-07-2000||04:26 PM||||JohnnyK, get this....I just finished stripping my wheels...they had been painted THREE times!!! I used Ace Hardware brand heavy duty paint stripper in a can. I swear, this is no b-s...I sprayed it on, it worked SO fast that the paint was literally falling off before I even made it all the way around the edge of the rim once! I swear it! My roommate owns an Ace Hardware here (thats how I get all my stuff  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) and we had been using all sorts of paint strippers, with little luck (slow). I said, "hey lets try the Ace brand"...so I grabbed a can, sprayed it.........OH MY GOD... I sprayed it once, the paint was falling off! I sprayed again some 10 seconds later and it was literally blowing the old paint right off! I swear by this stuff man!!!!!!!!! If you have an Ace Hardware around, get a can, you wont regret it! D@mn! I shouldve taken pics! Oh well.....||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnnyK||08-07-2000||05:15 PM||||Argh! Thats what I've been looking for!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Nope, no ace-hardware around here. But I just bought this Mar-somethingorother and I'm gonna try that!||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||08-07-2000||05:56 PM||||how fast it bubbles depends on what kind of paint is on them, enamel falls off, laquer has to be wire brushed , the stripper only softens laquer. I use aircraft grade stripper, from any auto paint store. DONT spray it ! the finest little specks in the air will ruin anything they land on. I stripped airplanes by spraying, but we stripped the whole thing, and in a hanger all by itself.||||reg||1
Z||000005||tgowens||08-07-2000||06:32 PM||||I have to agree with roger -- I used the aircraft stripper (gel) and I had no problems with the rims -- a soft brass brush, a little care and voila!! I would only use the spray if the wheels are off the car, the tires off the wheels, and you are in the middle of a big open field!!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/MY_SIGNATURE.gif">               <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||08-08-2000||02:01 AM||||Permatex Spray on Gasket Remover.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||08-08-2000||02:20 AM||||The "Mar-Hide" stuff doesn't work well. (In fact I think it S**KS) I used Permatex Spray on Gasket Remover. It works great! In 15 minutes the paint was gone. I have heard the Aircraft Stripper works well too just a little more hazardous than the gasket remover.||||reg||1
Z||000008||My7Fieros||08-08-2000||02:49 AM||||Roger and tg do have a point....I used the brush on aircraft stripper for the car. But when I did the wheels, I used the spray. However, I did take the wheels off the car first, and I made sure I was in an open space, so that the "splattering" wouldnt get on anything else. The brush on stuff works just as well, I just liked the spray stuff for some reason. The only problem I had with the spray stuff was that it didnt last long. It comes out w/ such force, that the can empties rather quickly. But I get the stuff for free, so it didnt bother me that much!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||JohnnyK||08-08-2000||03:07 PM||||Yup. That mar-hide stuff IS crap. Well, the gel works sort-of, but I found the spray on stuff doesn't. Even the mar-hide gel isn't that good, and I should get something better?||||reg||1
